rrelation computation) that asserts the computed values on a known input, not just that the pinned bug-corpus path is unperturbed.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1722,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'the existing pinned-corpus self-check still passes, proving the all-work extension did not perturb the shipped bug-corpus path'","'re-runs read (a) and reproduces its n (AC2)' — reproduction of n is not verification of the computed relationship","The new fragmentation/files-touched/correlation code paths are conditional logic, not pure scaffolding"],"finding":"The script extension adds new computational logic (files-touched extraction via `git show --name-only`, commit fragmentation grouping by `rebar-ticket:` trailer, and a new correlation/statistical layer) but the Testing section provides no test that asserts this new logic is correct — the `--check-planning-corpus` self-check only proves the pre-existing bug-corpus path did not regress, and AC2 proves reproducibility (same n on re-run) rather than correctness of the new variables or correlation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f763fd983086f44e3","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section; File impact: scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py (correlation layer)","norm_id":"n127dc9e9d0ef7a3f","priority":0.7778,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a test with a synthetic corpus of a few tickets whose files-touched, commit count, and rework signal are known, asserting the emitted distribution and correlation match hand-computed expected values.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State read (a)'s Gerrit patchset-count precondition and mechanism: name the auth/HTTPS requirement (bot Basic-auth over gerrit_base_url, per GerritClient), whether the backtest reuses `review_bot.gerrit_client.GerritClient` for the `o=ALL_REVISIONS` read, and how the run degrades when the token/network is absent so AC2 reproducibility still holds.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"patchset count from Gerrit `o=ALL_REVISIONS`, which is the cheapest per-change rework proxy and the only one requiring the network.\"","gerrit_client.py:106 builds Basic-auth from `bot_user:gerrit_bot_token`; startup.py:78 raises DecisionAuthError when gerrit_bot_token is missing/blank — the /a/ namespace read is credential-gated","gerrit_client.py:266 already uses `/a/changes/{id}?o=CURRENT_REVISION`; `o=ALL_REVISIONS` is a standard sibling option (Partially-verified: option value not directly observed in-repo, endpoint family + auth verified-in-use)","backtest_bugfix_size.py imports only git/subprocess helpers (lines 47-66); no Gerrit REST client is present, so the network read is a NEW surface for this script","ABSENCE: the plan states no auth/HTTPS precondition and no fallback for a token- or network-absent run, though AC2 requires read (a) to be reproducible"],"finding":"Read (a)'s patchset-count-from-Gerrit proxy is the plan's only network integration, but the plan neither states the auth/HTTPS precondition it requires nor names the mechanism the backtest script uses to reach Gerrit. The existing Gerrit REST access (review_bot.gerrit_client.GerritClient) authenticates against the /a/ namespace with bot Basic-auth (bot_user + gerrit_bot_token) over gerrit_base_url; backtest_bugfix_size.py today only shells `git` and has no REST client. The plan leaves unspecified whether it reuses GerritClient, requires those credentials to be present, and how it degrades when the token/network is absent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f042df83a20a8464c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Read (a): \"patchset count from Gerrit o=ALL_REVISIONS ... the only one requiring the network\"","norm_id":"n7fbbfdeda5feae54","priority":0.75,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or CI re-runs the documented read-(a) command (AC2) without gerrit_bot_token set — the patchset-count variable silently drops or the run errors, and the reported n is not reproducible","The script author has to invent a Gerrit REST call from scratch rather than reusing GerritClient, risking a divergent/unauthenticated code path"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Read (a), add: the patchset-count read reuses `rebar.review_bot.gerrit_client.GerritClient` (authenticated Basic-auth against the `/a/` namespace over `gerrit_base_url`, requiring `gerrit_bot_token`); when the credential/network is unavailable the run records patchset count as unavailable and the report's Method section documents the offline-vs-network variable set so AC2's n stays reproducible.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient",